输出格式为 JPEG 时，若某 JXL 无法通过 djxl 比特级还原为原始 J:
When the output format is JPEG, if a JXL cannot be bit-exactly rebuilt into the original JPG via djxl (e.g. non-JPEG source encoding, or rebuild data stripped), this switch decides how to handle it:
• Checked (mode A): skip the file directly and log the reason on the status page;
• Unchecked (default, mode B): show one confirmation, letting you decide whether to output it by "decoding to pixels then re-encoding to JPG" (lossy second-pass compression, quality drops).
